# Routes the @studiopod scope to GitHub Packages. Contains NO credential.
#
# Added in DS-7.5D, when this repository became a consumer of
# `@studiopod/foundation` for the first time. Before that it only *published*
# to this registry, which `publishConfig.registry` already handled, so no
# .npmrc was needed.
#
# Auth is deliberately NOT configured here. An `_authToken` line in a project
# .npmrc takes PRECEDENCE over the developer's ~/.npmrc and, whenever the
# referenced variable is unset, expands to an empty token and fails every
# install with E401 — observed in both consumer repositories during DS-7.4a and
# DS-7.4b, and corrected there. The token comes from the environment instead:
#
#   local dev : ~/.npmrc -> //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<read:packages PAT>
#   CI/Vercel : the build environment supplies npm auth for npm.pkg.github.com.
#               GitHub Packages requires a token for EVERY install, including
#               reads. See studiopod-web/DEPLOYMENT-OPS.md for the NPM_RC
#               mechanism — NPM_TOKEN alone does not cover a scoped registry.
#
# Publishing is unaffected: it stays pinned by package.json#publishConfig and
# the release workflow's own registry-url + scope.
@studiopod:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
